# Context

## Background
BehaviorModuleHost (packages/behavior-runtime/src/host.ts) spawns
process.execPath with the pack entrypoint and a minimal environment
{PATH, HOME, LANG, OAL_BEHAVIOR_CHILD: "1"}. The child must serve the
behavior protocol itself.

## Why This Way
The pack entry imports runBehaviorChild from
../../../packages/behavior-runtime/src/child.ts by relative path. A
bare specifier would resolve through package node_modules from the
importing file's own package, but the direct relative import keeps the
pack loadable without a build step and matches how the host resolves
the entry.

## Gotchas
- Without the marker gate, importing the pack entry in-process (tests,
  pack load) would start a child protocol listener on every import.
- The gateway still verifies a declared security alternative on every
  request even when pack security.enforce is false, so participants
  must send the minted credential (OAL_AUTH_BEARER) on every call.
